        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: Living Answers + action-form — the chat↔dashboard loop",
        "body": "> 📦 **Part of the modular-dashboard package** — master hub **#101136** (architecture diagrams · bottom-up merge order · the full per-PR test map).\n>\n> 🧪 **Try this PR:** add a `builtin:action-form` (`template: \"Deploy {env}\"`) and submit → it dispatches through the **same** operator-confirm + rate gate as the sandbox bridge; `ephemeral` answer-widgets self-sweep; **Pin** makes one permanent.\n\n---\n\n# Dashboard: Living Answers + action-form — the chat↔dashboard loop\n\n> Two halves of the flagship interaction: the agent answers show-don't-tell questions by composing a live widget, and widgets can act — a button or form that dispatches a parameterized prompt back to the agent.\n\nCloses #101820 and #101821. **Stacked on #101098** — targets `main` with a cumulative diff; review the `action-form`, `ephemeral`, and Living-Answers pieces as the delta.\n\n## What's in this PR\n- **`ephemeral` + pin (#101820)** — a widget may carry `ephemeral: { expiresAt }`; the store sweeps expired ephemeral widgets on read (one atomic write, only when something expired, version bumped), and a **Pin** action in the cell menu clears the marker to make it permanent. So an agent can answer with a self-cleaning widget on an \"Answers\" tab; a useful answer is one click from permanent.\n- **`builtin:action-form` (#101821)** — an operator-authored button/form whose fields interpolate into a `template` and submit dispatches it back to the agent. \"Deploy {env}\", \"Triage {id} as {priority}\" become one-click playbooks.\n- **Living-Answers convention** — an agent-facing doc (`extensions/dashboard/docs/LIVING-ANSWERS.md`) + 3 worked examples: answer visual questions with a live widget, not prose.\n\n## Security (action-form)\n- **No new dispatch privilege.** Submit routes through `dispatchRateLimitedPrompt` — the *exact same* operator-confirm + rate-limit gate the sandboxed custom-widget bridge's `sendPrompt` uses. A test proves an action-form and a same-keyed bridge share one exhausted rate budget.\n- **No template injection.** Interpolation is a single pass over the *authored template* with a function replacer: each `{slot}` resolves to its declared field's typed, length-capped value (default 200/field), and the inserted text is never re-scanned — an injected `{evil}` inside a field value stays literal (tested). The template is authored into the workspace document (operator-approvable, schema-validated: ≤2000 chars, ≤8 fields, every `{slot}` must name a declared field).\n\n## How it works\n\n**Dispatch flow — one shared gate, single-pass interpolation (the security argument, visual):**\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant W as action-form widget\n  participant P as Dashboard parent\n  participant G as dispatchRateLimitedPrompt (shared gate)\n  participant Chat as Agent / chat\n  W->>P: submit { field values }\n  P->>P: single-pass interpolate the AUTHORED template<br/>{slot} → typed, length-capped field · result never re-scanned\n  P->>G: dispatch(prompt)\n  G->>G: operator-confirm dialog + rate-limit<br/>(same budget as the sandbox bridge's sendPrompt — no new privilege)\n  G->>Chat: prompt (only if confirmed AND under budget)\n```\n\nThe `ephemeral` marker is a tiny schema addition swept in the store's existing read path; `action-form` is a trusted builtin registered like the others; the dispatch gate was extracted (`dispatchRateLimitedPrompt`) so the builtin and the sandbox bridge share one code path. No new dependency; no new gateway privilege.\n\nNote: this builds on the corrected base (#101098) where the UI↔gateway widget-mutation and file-binding contracts were fixed — pin uses the corrected `{ tab, id, patch }` mutation contract.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** The dashboard could show data but not *act*, and agent answers to visual questions were prose that died in the transcript. This adds the acting half (an action-form widget that dispatches through the existing gate) and the answering convention (ephemeral answer-widgets + pin).\n**Evidence:** `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/dashboard` + `pnpm vitest run src/lib/dashboard src/pages/plugin` green — schema validation (template/field caps, unknown-slot reject, ISO ephemeral), the store TTL sweep, the single-pass no-double-expansion interpolation, and the shared-rate-budget dispatch; `ui:i18n:check`, `ui:build`, full oxlint clean. Counts verified by the submitting orchestrator's own gate: `extensions/dashboard` 94, UI dashboard + plugin-page + cell suites 140.\n\n\n",
